          "hallucinations": false,
          "suggestions": "The agent correctly identified the oldest open corrective work order (1000052, CM, priority 3, FC006, no technician) and correctly excluded 1000051 as a PdM (non-corrective) order. It retrieved the correct sensor history for the window and identified all four samples as complete. The DGA classification (T2 thermal on both first and last samples, class unchanged) is consistent with the data, even though it fell back to manual IEC 60599 ratios after fmsr.interpret_dga reportedly failed. However, the anomaly screen (Finding 1) was never executed: the agent did not produce results from tsfm.run_recipe with an anomaly detector (and the visible trace shows no tsfm.data_quality or tsfm.find_models(task_id='tsfm_anomaly_detection') calls, only recipe_template). With 4 non-null samples per gas, the task explicitly required the model path, so the manual >50%-above-mean check offered 'for information only' does not satisfy the requirement. Because Finding 1 was incomplete, the decision rule could not be applied and no work order action was taken; while the agent was honest and conservative rather than fabricating results, the task was not completed. To rectify: call tsfm.find_models(task_id='tsfm_anomaly_detection'), run tsfm.data_quality and tsfm.run_recipe on hydrogen, ethylene and acetylene (writing the series to the required data input if the recipe needs a file path), then apply the decision logic \u2014 given the stable T2 class and no outliers in the last two samples, the expected outcome would likely be closing 1000052 via wo.close_workorder with both findings in the resolution notes and failure code FC006 retained."
